# Optional. Everything has a safe default; the lab needs no tenant and no credentials (it holds none).
# The shared settings file is ~/Development/.env (mode 600; STANDALONE_ENV overrides the path), read by every standalone app.
# This lab reads one optional key from it:
# CAL_LAB_MODE=mock               # the mode a new workspace opens in: mock (default) or live (live is refused until step 3)
# Per-run settings (shell, not the shared file; the shared file holds no PORT):
# PORT=5600                       # must be in 5600-5699 (Docker publishes 5601 by default)
# CALAB_BIND=127.0.0.1            # loopback only unless you set this on purpose (the container does)
# ALLOW_MOCK_SIGNIN=1             # the owner's opt-in to the mock persona sign-in (scripts/run.sh and Docker set it)
# IDP=mock                        # mock (default). Anything else turns mock sign-in off.
# CAL_ALLOW_LIVE=1                # the owner's opt-in to SELECT live mode (needs IDP set to a live provider). Live runs are not built yet.
